    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Nestled in a tranquil lakeside setting in the heart of County Leitrim, No. 9 Lakeside Cottage is a charming detached residence offering the perfect blend of comfort, privacy, and natural beauty. Set amidst beautifully maintained grounds with mature trees and expansive green spaces, this attractive stone-fronted home enjoys a peaceful countryside atmosphere while remaining conveniently accessible to nearby towns and amenities.\r\nThe property is thoughtfully designed to provide bright and spacious accommodation, with well-proportioned living areas and generous bedroom accommodation ideal for families, holidaymakers, or those seeking a relaxing rural retreat. \r\nLocated close to the shores of Lough Scur, the property offers easy access to fishing, boating, walking trails, and a wide range of outdoor pursuits. The nearby towns of Drumshanbo, Carrick-on-Shannon, and Ballinamore provide excellent shopping, dining, and recreational facilities, making this an ideal base for both permanent living and holiday enjoyment. The accommodation comprises a kitchenette, spacious Living room, Bathroom, No 3 Bedrooms (1 ensuite). \r\nNo. 9 Lakeside Cottage presents a rare opportunity to acquire a beautifully positioned property in one of Leitrim's most scenic and peaceful locations. Viewing Strictly by Appointment Only with Sole Selling Agent."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Kitchenette\r\nLiving room\r\nBathroom\r\nNo 3 Bedrooms (1 ensuite)."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Attractive detached stone-fronted cottage\r\nSpacious and bright accommodation throughout\r\nGenerous landscaped grounds\r\nPeaceful lakeside setting\r\nSurrounded by mature trees and countryside views\r\nClose to Lough Scur and outdoor recreational amenities\r\nConvenient access to Drumshanbo, Ballinamore, and Carrick-on-Shannon\r\nIdeal as a family home, holiday residence, or investment property\r\nYear built 2006"
      },
